# Prompt Engineering Best Practices

## Prompt Design
- Keep prompts clear, specific, and concise
- Use structured input formats
- Include clear instructions and constraints
- Avoid ambiguous language and excessive context
- Define output formats and expected results
- Organize prompt parts in a logical order
- Use examples to illustrate expected behavior (learning with a small number of examples)
- Guide complex reasoning with step-by-step instructions

## Prompt Optimization
- Iteratively test and improve prompts
- Analyze prompt performance and success rate
- Record prompt iteration history
- Build a prompt template library
- Identify and eliminate ambiguities
- Use prompt links to decompose complex tasks
- Optimize token usage efficiency
- Verify compatibility of different model versions

## Prompt Security
- Avoid including sensitive information in prompts
- Use abstract instructions to avoid information leakage
- Prevent prompt injection attacks
- Implement prompt verification mechanisms
- Identify and exclude potentially harmful outputs
- Implement content filtering and auditing
- Follow safe prompt design principles
- Limit prompt permissions and access scope

## Prompt Version Control
- Maintain prompt version history
- Document the purpose and effect of each change
- Establish benchmark performance tests for each version
- Support rollback to previous prompt versions
- Use naming conventions and version numbers
- Document compatibility of models and prompts
- Implement prompt review process
- Save mapping of prompts to corresponding model versions

## Context Window Management
- Optimize prompts to fit context window limitations
- Implement context compression and summarization techniques
- Design dynamic context management strategies
- Use external knowledge bases to extend context
- Identify and prioritize key information
- Implement context window segmentation strategies
- Use efficient encoding and structure
- Monitor and optimize context window usage

## Prompt Composition and Modularity
- Build a library of reusable prompt components
- Define standard prompt templates
- Implement prompt parameterization and dynamic generation
- Decompose complex prompts into manageable modules
- Use prompt composition to solve multi-step problems
- Define cross-prompt standards and conventions
- Design domain-specific prompt modules
- Implement prompt inheritance and extension mechanisms

## Prompt Evaluation and Analysis
- Establish evaluation criteria for prompt quality
- Conduct systematic prompt comparison and benchmarking
- Analyze prompt performance bottlenecks
- Collect and integrate user feedback
- Identify interaction patterns between models and prompts
- Implement an automated prompt evaluation pipeline
- Track prompt evolution and performance trends
- Use prompt analysis to improve designs